.TH GRAINULATOR 1
.SH NAME
grainulator \- evidence and execution tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grainulator
command [options]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create an evidence sprint without changing host settings.
.TP
.B add
Append a typed evidence claim.
.TP
.B import
Import active document findings.
.TP
.B compile
Validate and compile evidence.
.TP
.B status
Inspect sprint health.
.TP
.B search
Search recorded evidence.
.TP
.B resolve
Resolve a claim conflict.
.TP
.B guard
Check a proposed write against evidence requirements.
.TP
.B stats
Inspect local sprint statistics.
.TP
.B maintain
Maintain premises, observations, findings and acceptance.
.TP
.B report
Freeze and check grounded report packets.
.TP
.B research
Run or resume an exported research session.
.TP
.B memory
Store, search and reuse local knowledge.
.TP
.B export
Convert evidence into shareable artifacts.
.TP
.B analytics
Inspect sprint metrics and retrospectives.
.TP
.B orchestrate
Coordinate related sprints.
.TP
.B runtime
Explicit native convergence operations and installation.
.TP
.B utils
Shared asset and manifest utilities.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect the installed build and local configuration.
.TP
.B config
Check and explain project configuration.
.TP
.B demo
Run a synthetic offline repair and verifier example.
.TP
.B run
Attach a command adapter to a bounded task loop.
.TP
.B setup
Save a default native-host workspace binding.
.TP
.B connect
Print an explicit MCP registration.
.TP
.B mcp
Start the unified local MCP server.
.TP
.B preview
Open the local research playground.
.TP
.B completion
Print a static bash, zsh or fish completion script.
.TP
.B man
Print the offline command reference.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit statuses are command-specific. The adapter run returns 0 for verified, 2 for an unverified terminal outcome, 3 for a soundness break and 1 for usage/configuration errors. Native runtime and Stop hook protocols have distinct statuses; see their command help.
.SH DATA
Project configuration is grainulator.config.json. Evidence claims.json and compilation.json remain generic filenames. User data is retained when the package is removed.
.SH SEE ALSO
Run grainulator command --help.
